{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-associative-and-animate-restriction","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--animacy-debate"],"statement":{"en":"The plural marker utar does not necessarily express multiple identical items but can convey an associative plural meaning ('X and company'), which is restricted to animates.","ja":"複数標識 utar は必ずしも同一物の複数倍を表すのではなく連想複数（「Xとその仲間」）を表すことができ、その用法は有情物に限定される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["utar","acha utar arki"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0044-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-incompatible-with-inanimate-nouns","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--animacy-debate"],"statement":{"en":"The plural marker utar cannot attach to inanimate nouns such as shuma 'stone' or ni 'tree'.","ja":"複数標識 utar は shuma「石」や ni「木」のような無情名詞に後続することはできない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"none","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["shuma utar","ni utar","utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0045-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contradicts","claim":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun-inanimate-use","differs_in":"unresolved","note":"Kindaichi & Chiri claim utar cannot attach to inanimate nouns like shuma or ni, whereas Nakagawa states utar can attach to inanimates, citing suma utar and ni utar."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-shizunai-animacy-hierarchy","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--animacy-debate"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai Ainu, the suffix -utar is widely used for humans, rare for animals, and never occurs with inanimates.","ja":"静内アイヌ語において、接尾辞 -utar は人間に対しては広く用いられ、動物には稀であり、無生物には決して用いられない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0152-10","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-incompatible-with-inanimate-nouns","differs_in":null,"note":"Refsing's corpus findings corroborate the claim that utar does not occur with inanimate nouns."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-with-non-human-animates","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--animacy-debate"],"statement":{"en":"The plural marker utar can be placed after nouns denoting non-human living things to express plurality.","ja":"複数標識 utar は人間以外の生物を表す名詞の後に置かれて複数を表すことがある。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0315-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--hekattar-formation-and-reduplication","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--hekattar"],"statement":{"en":"The noun hekachi 'child' combines with utar to form the lexicalized plural hekattar, which can further take utar again as hekattar utar.","ja":"名詞 hekachi「子」は utar が付いて複数形 hekattar「子ども」となり、さらに utar を付加して hekattar utar とすることもできる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["hekachi","utar","hekattar","hekattar utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0045-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-plural-suffixes-as-determiners","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"Pluralizing nominal suffixes such as 'utah and 'oy in Sakhalin Ainu are classified as post-nominal determiners.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語における 'utah や 'oy などの名詞複数接尾辞は、連体後詞（det）に分類される。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["'utah","'oy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0007-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-utah-plural-suffix","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, 'utah functions as a plural suffix meaning '-people, -s'.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において、'utah は「～たち」を意味する複数接尾辞として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["'utah"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0066-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-elder-speech-plural-marking","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"In the elder register of Sakhalin Ainu, plural forms are pervasive across both nouns and verbs.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語の老人言葉では、名詞・動詞を問わず全般的に複数形が用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"most","modality":"assertive","conditions":["elder register"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0094-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-specific-possessive-plural-hcin","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"The possessive plural suffix -hcin is unique to Sakhalin Ainu and does not exist in Hokkaido Ainu.","ja":"所属複数接尾辞 -hcin は北海道アイヌ語には見られず、樺太アイヌ語特有のものである。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-hcin"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0107-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-plural-marking-by-belonging","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, plural marking fundamentally distinguishes whether a group belongs to someone or something, using -hcin for possessed groups.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語では、複数の集団が何かに所属しているか否かで文法標示が根本的に異なり、所属している集団には -hcin が用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-hcin"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-uta-non-large-plural-distribution","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, 'uta(h) / 'utara expresses a moderate plural and, unlike in Hokkaido, can occur with all non-affiliative nouns rather than only human nouns.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において 'uta(h) 〜 'utara は多数ではない複数を表し、北海道と異なり人間だけでなく所属形以外のすべての名詞に使える。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["non-affiliative noun"]},"forms":["'uta","'utah","'utara"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0109-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-incompatible-with-inanimate-nouns","differs_in":"dialect","note":"Murasaki notes that unlike Hokkaido utar, Sakhalin 'uta(h) is not restricted to humans and can be used with all non-affiliative nouns."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-oy-large-plural","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, the post-nominal determiner 'oy denotes a larger number of referents than 'uta(h).","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において、連体後詞 'oy は 'uta(h) より多数の複数を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["'oy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0109-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-ikiri-crowd-plural","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, the post-nominal determiner 'ikiri denotes an even larger crowd or host than 'oy.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において、連体後詞 'ikiri は 'oy よりもさらに多い集団や群れを表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["'ikiri"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0110-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--nominal-plural-contrast-hokkaido-sakhalin","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"Hokkaido Ainu nouns do not distinguish singular and plural forms, whereas Sakhalin Ainu forms plurals by suffixing -(a)hcin / -(a)hsin.","ja":"北海道アイヌ語の名詞には単複の区別がないのに対し、樺太アイヌ語では接辞 -(a)hcin（または -(a)hsin）を付加して複数形を形成する。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-(a)hcin","-(a)hsin"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-ahcin-non-grammatical-number","differs_in":"level-of-analysis","note":"Nakagawa (p.110) presents Sakhalin -(a)hcin as a nominal plural forming device contrasting with Hokkaido, but later (p.261) argues that -(a)hcin is not an exponent of grammatical nominal number."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-noun-plural-suffixes-inventory","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"Sakhalin Ainu has the nominal plural suffixes -(a)hcin (Western), -(a)hsin (Eastern), and -utah ~ -utara.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語には、複数を表す名詞接尾辞として -(a)hcin（西海岸）、-(a)hsin（東海岸）、および -utah 〜 -utara が存在する。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-(a)hcin","-(a)hsin","-utah","-utara"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0256-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-ahcin-homogeneous-vs-utara-associative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, -(a)hcin expresses strictly homogeneous plurality on affiliative forms or nominalizers, whereas -uta(ra) can express either homogeneous or associative plurality.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において、-(a)hcin は所属形や名詞化辞に付いて同質複数のみを表すのに対し、-uta(ra) は同質複数または連想複数の両方を表すことができる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-(a)hcin","-ahcin","-utara","-uta"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0257-01","stance":"reports"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0258-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-ahcin-non-grammatical-number","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"The Sakhalin Ainu plural suffix -(a)hcin cannot be analyzed as an exponent of a grammatical category of nominal number, since it is not obligatory and can attach to complementizers.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語の複数接尾辞 -(a)hcin は、義務的でなく補文標識にも付加できるため、名詞の文法的な数範疇の指標とは見なしがたい。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-(a)hcin"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0258-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-hcin-possessor-or-possessee-plural","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, the affiliative form takes -hcin when either the possessor or the possessed entity is plural.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において、所属形は所有者または被所有者のいずれかが複数である場合に接尾辞 -hcin を取る。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-hcin"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:tangiku2022@handbook-epub/l0057-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-hcin-affiliative-restriction","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, the plural suffix -hcin attaches exclusively to the affiliative (possessed) form of nouns.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において、名詞複数接尾辞 -hcin は所属形にのみ後続する。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-hcin"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:tangiku2022@handbook-epub/l0059-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-hcin-plural-possessor-agreement","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, when there are multiple possessors and a singular possessee, -hcin attaches after the affiliative suffix to agree with the plural possessor.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において、所有者が複数で被所有物が単数の場合、所属形接尾辞の後に -hcin が付加されて複数所有者との一致を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["plural possessor","singular possessee"]},"forms":["-hcin"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:tangiku2022@handbook-epub/l0059-16","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-hcin-plural-possessee-agreement","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--sakhalin-contrast"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, when there is a single possessor and multiple possessees, -hcin attaches after the affiliative suffix to agree with the plural possessees.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において、所有者が単数で被所有物が複数の場合、所属形接尾辞の後に付加された -hcin は複数被所有物との一致を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["singular possessor","plural possessee"]},"forms":["-hcin"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:tangiku2022@handbook-epub/l0059-17","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--bare-nouns-transnumeral","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--transnumerality"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu nouns do not distinguish singular and plural by themselves; a bare noun form represents both singular and plural referents.","ja":"アイヌ語の名詞は単独では単複の区別を持たず、単一の形式で単数と複数の両方を表す。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["ainu","shuma"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0044-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--inherent-plurals-expressed-by-reduplication","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--transnumerality"],"statement":{"en":"Entities that inherently exist in the plural are lexicalized through reduplication in Ainu.","ja":"常に複数的に存在している事物は、畳語法によって語彙化されて表現される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["chaichai","kaukau","kaikai","kankan","merimeri","paspas","pisepise","ramram","taktak","tuntun","toitoi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0045-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--morphological-number-absent-on-nouns","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--transnumerality"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu does not mark nouns morphologically for number, with morphological singular/plural distinctions occurring only on verbs.","ja":"アイヌ語は名詞に形態的な数標示を行わず、単数と複数の形態的区別は動詞にのみ見られる。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022@handbook-epub/l0110-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--hokkaido-nominal-grammatical-number-absence","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--transnumerality"],"statement":{"en":"In Hokkaido Ainu dialects, nouns lack a grammatical category of number, with no form that obligatorily marks singular versus plural.","ja":"アイヌ語北海道方言には名詞に文法的な数の区別（単数形・複数形）がなく、単数か複数かを義務的に示す形式は存在しない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0256-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--morphological-number-absent-on-nouns","differs_in":"scope","note":"Nakagawa restricts the claim of lack of grammatical number to Hokkaido dialects in contrast to Sakhalin."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--general-nouns-unmarked-except-reduplication","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--transnumerality"],"statement":{"en":"Number on general nouns is unmarked, except for a few cases marked by reduplication.","ja":"一般名詞における数は少数の畳語による例外を除き標示されない。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"most","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0074-14","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--shizunai-nominal-number-emphasis","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--transnumerality"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai Ainu, nouns are generally unmarked for number, but plurality may be emphasized by reduplication or by suffixing -utar.","ja":"静内アイヌ語において名詞類は通常数標示を持たないが、畳語化または接尾辞 -utar の付加によって複数を強調できる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0152-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--full-nouns-lack-number-and-agreement","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--transnumerality"],"statement":{"en":"Full nouns lack grammatical number inflection, and there is no number agreement within the noun phrase.","ja":"完全名詞には数の文法範疇が存在せず、複数語形変化も名詞句内の数一致も存在しない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["sine aynu","tu aynu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0025-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-collective-noun-meaning","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun"],"statement":{"en":"In collective nominal usage, the noun 'utár refers to '(Ainu) people'.","ja":"集合名詞的な用法において、名詞 'utár は「（アイヌの）人々」を指す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["'utár"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:janhunen2022@handbook-epub/l0010-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-particle-plural-marking","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun"],"statement":{"en":"The particle utar is placed after nouns when plural number is explicitly indicated.","ja":"名詞の複数を特に明示したい場合には助詞 utar が用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0044-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun-inanimate-use","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun"],"statement":{"en":"The formal noun utar marks nominal plurality explicitly and can occur with inanimate nouns like suma utar 'stones' and ni utar 'trees'.","ja":"形式名詞 utar は名詞に後続して複数を明示し、suma utar「石たち」や ni utar「木たち」のように無生物名詞に対しても用いることができる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0256-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-suffix-sparse-marking","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun"],"statement":{"en":"Number on general nouns is marked only in a few cases by the suffix -utar.","ja":"一般名詞における数は、少数の事例で接尾辞 -utar によって標示される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"few","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0074-13","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--shizunai-utar-with-non-singular-numerals","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai Ainu, nouns that can take the plural suffix -utar generally do so when quantified by numerals greater than one.","ja":"静内アイヌ語において、複数接尾辞 -utar を取り得る名詞は、「1」以外の数詞で修飾されると通常この接尾辞を伴う。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"most","modality":"assertive","conditions":["modified by numeral > 1"]},"forms":["-utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0110-07","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0111-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--shizunai-utar-on-personal-pronouns","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai Ainu, the suffix -utar attaches to personal pronouns to form plural pronouns.","ja":"静内アイヌ語において、接尾辞 -utar は人称代名詞に付加されて複数形を形成する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0152-11","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--shizunai-utar-plural-nominalizer","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai Ainu, -utar functions as a plural nominalizer when suffixed to verbal stems.","ja":"静内アイヌ語において、-utar は動詞類に付加されて複数名詞化辞として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0152-12","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--shizunai-nominalizing-utar-human-only","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun"],"statement":{"en":"When functioning as a nominalizer on verbal stems in Shizunai Ainu, -utar exclusively refers to human beings.","ja":"静内アイヌ語で名詞化辞として機能する場合、-utar は常に人間全般のみを指す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["nominalizer function"]},"forms":["-utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0154-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-appositive-noun-plurality","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun"],"statement":{"en":"In addition to clausal modification, utar can stand in apposition to a noun to express nominal plurality.","ja":"utar には節修飾を受ける用法のほかに、名詞と同格に置かれて複数を表す用法もある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0198-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-suffix-plural-and-associative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-formal-noun"],"statement":{"en":"The suffix -utar can attach to nouns to express plurality or an associative reading ('X and others').","ja":"名詞に接尾辞 -utar を付加することで、複数性または「Xとその仲間」という連想複数を表すことができる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-utar","aynu-utar","cip-utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0025-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--shizunai-utar-ordering-associative-inside","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-utari"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai Ainu, placing -utar inside the possessive suffix (e.g. a=yup-utar-i) marks associative plural, whereas placing utar outside (e.g. a=yup-i utar) marks regular plural.","ja":"静内アイヌ語において、-utar が所属形接尾辞の内側に入る場合（a=yup-utar-i）は連想複数を表し、外側に置かれる場合（a=yup-i utar）は通常の複数を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-utar","utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2015@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0016-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contradicts","claim":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--shibatani-utar-ordering-regular-inside","differs_in":"unresolved","note":"Bugaeva asserts that -utar inside the possessive suffix yields an associative plural and outside yields a regular plural, whereas Shibatani asserts the exact reverse."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-derived-from-utari","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-utari"],"statement":{"en":"The plural suffix -utar historically derives from the noun utari 'friend, fellow Ainu, relative'.","ja":"複数接尾辞 -utar は名詞 utari「友人、同胞、親族」に由来する。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-utar","utari"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0152-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-noun-and-affiliative-utari","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-utari"],"statement":{"en":"The noun utar means 'relatives', and utari functions as its affiliative (possessed) form.","ja":"名詞 utar は「親戚」を意味し、utari はその所属形である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["utar","utari"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0198-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--shibatani-utar-ordering-regular-inside","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--utar-utari"],"statement":{"en":"Placing -utar inside the possessive suffix marks plural possession ('my older brothers', ku-yup-utar-i), whereas placing -utar outside marks associative plural possession ('my older brother and others', ku-yup-i-utar).","ja":"-utar が所属形接尾辞の内側にある形（ku-yup-utar-i）は「私の兄たち」という複数所属を表し、外側にある形（ku-yup-i-utar）は「兄とその仲間」という連想複数を表す。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-utar","ku-yup-utar-i","ku-yup-i-utar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0025-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--noun-number-expressed-by-verb","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--verbal-number"],"statement":{"en":"Because Ainu nouns do not inflect for number while verbs distinguish singular and plural stems, the number of a noun is generally signaled by its associated verb.","ja":"アイヌ語の名詞は単複で語形変化しないが動詞は単数語幹と複数語幹を区別するため、名詞の数は一般に関連する動詞によって示される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0079-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--numeral-blocks-verbal-plural-marking","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--verbal-number"],"statement":{"en":"When the number of a noun is explicitly indicated by a numeral, the verb need not mark plural and remains in the singular stem.","ja":"名詞の数が数詞によって明示されている場合、動詞は複数形を取る必要がなく単数形のままとなる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["quantified by numeral"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0079-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--verbal-number-distinction-in-ainu","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality","topic:nominal/nominal-number-utar-transnumerality--verbal-number"],"statement":{"en":"Although Ainu nouns lack a grammatical number category, certain verbs distinguish singular and plural stems (verbal number).","ja":"アイヌ語の名詞には文法的な数の範疇が存在しないが、一部の動詞には単数形と複数形の語幹対立（動詞数）が存在する。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0137-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
